<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The app's forensic trail: one file, %AppData%\FocusDesk\Logs\app.log. Retention and size live
  HERE, not in code, so they can be changed on an installed machine without a rebuild.

  Loaded automatically by NLog from beside the exe (see Services/AppLog.cs). If this file is missing
  or unparseable, nothing is logged at all — the reasoning is in AppLog's remarks.
-->
<nlog xmlns="http://www.nlog-project.org/schemas/NLog.xsd"
      xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      internalLogLevel="Off">

  <targets>
    <!--
      Four traps measured against a sibling project's own concurrent-writer regression, carried over
      here because the same shape of failure — several FocusDesk processes appending to one file —
      applies unchanged:

      Trap 1 — keepFileOpen. NLog's DEFAULT, keepFileOpen="true", holds an exclusive handle and a
      sibling process's concurrent writes are silently lost — NLog reports none of it, not even to
      its own internal log. keepFileOpen="false" makes NLog open the file per write with a share mode
      that tolerates other writers, paired with the RetryingWrapper below to ride out a collision
      rather than drop the line.
    -->
    <target name="appfile" xsi:type="RetryingWrapper" retryCount="5" retryDelayMilliseconds="20">
      <!--
      Trap 2 — the removed attribute. Do NOT "restore" concurrentWrites="true" here. That was NLog
      5's name for this behaviour; NLog 6 REMOVED the property, and an unknown attribute is silently
      ignored unless throwConfigExceptions is on — so it would look correct, do nothing, and lose
      lines exactly as the default keepFileOpen does.

      Rotation: archiveEvery="Day" moves the active file to app_<date>_00.log at the first write
      after midnight (NLog probes the file's birth time), maxArchiveFiles="7" keeps the seven most
      recent archives, and archiveAboveSize stays as a within-day guard.

      Trap 3 — archive counting. Do NOT swap maxArchiveFiles for maxArchiveDays. Measured: it judges
      an archive by its CREATION time, and Windows preserves creation time when the active file is
      moved to its archive name. A log file created weeks ago is therefore archived and deleted in
      the same write, so an upgrade destroys the existing app.log and a week of downtime destroys
      that week. maxArchiveFiles counts archives instead and survives both.

      NLog 6 renamed this area too: archiveNumbering and archiveDateFormat are OBSOLETE in 6.1.4 and
      archiveSuffixFormat replaces both, so a config written in NLog 5's idiom parses and rotates
      nothing.

      The layout has NO trailing newline. lineEnding="LF" already terminates the entry; carrying
      both put a blank line between every pair of entries. The class column comes from an event
      property the AppLog facade fills from [CallerFilePath] — free, and correct across async
      boundaries, where ${callsite} costs 2.2x per entry and reports the facade instead of the caller.

      The timestamp carries milliseconds so ordering inside one second stays resolvable.

      Trap 4 — the date culture. ${date} has NO culture= parameter because NLog's ${date} already
      defaults to InvariantCulture, and this timestamp is machine-facing log data that must stay
      Gregorian/ASCII on every locale. Do not "fix" the apparent omission by adding culture="" — an
      EMPTY culture makes NLog fall back to the thread's CurrentCulture, which stamps a non-Gregorian
      year under some locales (measured: 1448-02-03 under ar-SA on the sibling project this config
      is drawn from). culture=Invariant is not a thing and throws.
      -->
      <target name="appfile_file"
              xsi:type="File"
              fileName="${specialfolder:folder=ApplicationData}\FocusDesk\Logs\app.log"
              keepFileOpen="false"
              createDirs="true"
              encoding="utf-8"
              writeBom="false"
              archiveAboveSize="10485760"
              archiveEvery="Day"
              maxArchiveFiles="7"
              archiveSuffixFormat="_{1:yyyy-MM-dd}_{0:00}"
              lineEnding="LF"
              layout="[${date:format=yyyy-MM-dd HH\:mm\:ss.fff zzz}] ${level:uppercase=true:padding=-5} ${pad:padding=-24:inner=${event-properties:item=class:whenEmpty=-}} ${message}" />
    </target>
  </targets>

  <rules>
    <logger name="*" minlevel="Info" writeTo="appfile" />
  </rules>
</nlog>
